---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { PILLARS } from '../data/aoh';

/* The depth for each pillar, in the same order as PILLARS. Copy from the
   previous framework page. */
const DEPTH = [
  {
    intro: 'The foundation everything else is built on.',
    body: [
      'Physical vitality is not vanity, it is infrastructure. The quality of someone’s sleep, their movement habits, their relationship with food and alcohol, their physical energy levels: these are not lifestyle choices that sit outside the conversation about performance. They are the conversation.',
      'When this pillar is under strain, everything else suffers. Concentration drops. Emotional regulation becomes harder. Relationships feel more difficult. Work feels heavier. Restoring physical vitality doesn’t just improve health metrics, it creates the conditions for every other pillar to function.',
      'In our work with organisations, Health & Fitness is often the pillar people find easiest to engage with first. It’s concrete. It’s measurable. And the wins here, even small ones, create momentum that carries into the others.',
    ],
    practices: ['Movement habits and exercise consistency', 'Sleep quality and recovery', 'Nutrition and energy management', 'Relationship with alcohol and substances', 'Physical presence and body–mind connection'],
  },
  {
    intro: 'The pillar most people skip, and the one with the biggest upstream influence.',
    body: [
      'Internal Work is the hardest pillar to talk about and the most important one to address. It covers self-awareness, emotional intelligence, values clarity, identity, and the internal narratives people carry about who they are and what they’re capable of.',
      'Most people arrive at adulthood with a set of beliefs about themselves that were formed in childhood and never examined. Those beliefs shape how they respond to pressure, how they relate to others, whether they ask for help, and whether they feel they deserve a fulfilling life. In the workplace they show up as patterns: the manager who can’t delegate, the high performer who can’t switch off, the leader who avoids difficult conversations.',
      'This is not therapy. It is structured self-inquiry, the kind that gives people language for what they’re experiencing and tools to shift what isn’t serving them.',
    ],
    practices: ['Values identification and alignment', 'Emotional awareness and regulation', 'Recognising limiting beliefs', 'Purpose and identity work', 'Mindset and self-talk patterns'],
  },
  {
    intro: 'The quality of our closest connections shapes everything.',
    body: [
      'The quality of a person’s intimate relationships is one of the strongest predictors of their overall wellbeing, mental health and even physical longevity. And yet it is almost never addressed in workplace wellbeing programs, as if the most important relationship in someone’s life stops mattering from nine to five.',
      'It doesn’t. A marriage in crisis affects concentration, emotional stability and capacity for patience. A relationship built on genuine support and security creates a stability that makes everything else more possible. This pillar is not about prying into personal lives. It is about acknowledging that the whole person shows up to work, and that supporting the whole person means taking this seriously.',
      'For single people, this pillar addresses relationship readiness, attachment patterns, and the quality of connection being sought and experienced.',
    ],
    practices: ['Communication and conflict resolution', 'Emotional intimacy and vulnerability', 'Attachment awareness', 'Relationship values and expectations', 'Support systems within partnerships'],
  },
  {
    intro: 'Loneliness is one of the strongest predictors of declining health and performance. It’s also one of the least discussed.',
    body: [
      'Beyond our intimate relationships sits a broader layer of connection: friendships, community, belonging and the social fabric of everyday life. This is the pillar that has eroded most dramatically in the modern world. People have more digital contacts and fewer genuine friendships than at any point in recent history.',
      'In men specifically, this pillar is in crisis. Research consistently shows that men’s social networks shrink dramatically after their mid-twenties, and that the absence of meaningful male friendship is a significant driver of the mental health challenges that eventually surface as crisis.',
      'In organisations, this pillar shows up in how psychologically safe people feel, how connected they feel to their colleagues, and whether they experience their workplace as a genuine community or simply a transaction.',
    ],
    practices: ['Depth and quality of friendships', 'Sense of belonging and community', 'Ability to ask for help', 'Social confidence and connection rituals', 'Workplace belonging and psychological safety'],
  },
  {
    intro: 'Not balance. Integration.',
    body: [
      'Work–life balance implies a scale, as if work and life were two opposing forces to be managed against each other. That framing is both inaccurate and demoralising. The question is not how to do less of one and more of the other. It is how to design a life where professional contribution and personal fulfilment reinforce each other rather than compete.',
      'This pillar covers purpose in work, the experience of meaning and flow, boundary-setting, career alignment with values, and the quality of life outside work: whether there are enough things beyond the job that matter, replenish and sustain.',
      'For many people this is the pillar they arrive at last, because it needs the other four to be stable enough to examine clearly. But it is also the pillar that connects most directly to what organisations call engagement, discretionary effort and retention.',
    ],
    practices: ['Purpose and meaning in work', 'Work–life integration rather than conflict', 'Boundary-setting and recovery', 'Career alignment with personal values', 'Fulfilment and engagement outside work'],
  },
];
const pillars = PILLARS.map((p, i) => ({ ...p, ...DEPTH[i] }));

/* Real-life chains: indexes into PILLARS. */
const EXAMPLES = [
  {
    says: '“I’m too busy to exercise right now.”',
    body: 'When Work & Life Flow is under pressure, Health & Fitness is usually the first thing sacrificed. Less movement leads to lower energy, which makes the workload feel heavier, which leads to longer hours, and the cycle compounds. This is not a discipline problem. It is a systems problem.',
    chain: [4, 0, 1],
  },
  {
    says: '“I can’t concentrate today.”',
    body: 'A difficult conversation at home the night before doesn’t stay at home. Emotional residue from conflict consumes cognitive bandwidth, reduces patience with colleagues and makes even routine decisions feel harder. Supporting Love & Relationships isn’t a personal indulgence. It directly affects professional output.',
    chain: [2, 1, 4],
  },
  {
    says: '“He seems fine, just a bit checked out.”',
    body: 'Someone who has gradually lost their social connections outside work, friends drifted, social life contracted, may appear functional but is running on empty. Work becomes both their only source of social contact and the place they feel most disconnected. Engagement scores drop. The cause is invisible.',
    chain: [3, 1, 4],
  },
];

/* Every format we deliver, from one room to every month. */
const FORMATS = [
  { href: '/what-we-do/keynotes-workshops', icon: 'mic', tag: '45 min to a full day', title: 'Keynotes & workshops', text: 'The framework live in the room. People score themselves and leave with one clear action.' },
  { href: '/what-we-do/masterclass', icon: 'board', tag: '60–90 min', title: 'Masterclass', text: 'Your leadership team’s first experience of the framework, and a clear read on where your culture sits.' },
  { href: '/what-we-do/wellness-accelerator', icon: 'climb', tag: '6 weeks', title: 'Wellness Accelerator', text: 'All five pillars, with structure, accountability and measurable outcomes.' },
  { href: '/what-we-do/leadership-coaching', icon: 'talk', tag: '1:1', title: 'Leadership coaching', text: 'The framework applied one to one, for leaders who want to model it.' },
  { href: '/what-we-do/culture-consulting', icon: 'compass', tag: 'Partnership', title: 'Culture consulting', text: 'We diagnose what’s really going on, build the system to shift it, and stay until it holds.' },
] as const;

// Pentagon geometry (as on the home page).
const corner = (cx: number, cy: number, r: number, i: number) => {
  const a = (Math.PI * 2 * i) / 5 - Math.PI / 2;
  return [cx + r * Math.cos(a), cy + r * Math.sin(a)];
};
const pts = (cx: number, cy: number, r: (i: number) => number) => [0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map(i => corner(cx, cy, r(i), i));
const svgPts = (p: number[][]) => p.map(([x, y]) => `${x.toFixed(1)},${y.toFixed(1)}`).join(' ');

// The explorer: five corners, every pillar joined to every other.
const PX = { w: 400, h: 420, cx: 200, cy: 196, r: 146 };
const pxC = pts(PX.cx, PX.cy, () => PX.r);
const pxLines: { a: number; b: number; edge: boolean }[] = [];
for (let a = 0; a < 5; a++) for (let b = a + 1; b < 5; b++) pxLines.push({ a, b, edge: b - a === 1 || b - a === 4 });
const pct = (v: number, of: number) => ((v / of) * 100).toFixed(2) + '%';

// The check-in visual: an example shape across the five pillars.
const CI = { cx: 160, cy: 160, r: 104 };
const EXAMPLE = [70, 48, 76, 56, 62];
const ciRings = [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1].map(s => svgPts(pts(CI.cx, CI.cy, () => CI.r * s)));
const ciShape = pts(CI.cx, CI.cy, i => CI.r * EXAMPLE[i] / 100);
const ciIcons = pts(CI.cx, CI.cy, () => CI.r + 30);
---
<Base title="The Five Pillars of Fulfilment · The Artistry of Humanity" description="The Five Pillars of Fulfilment is The Artistry of Humanity’s framework for human wellbeing: Health & Fitness, Internal Work, Love & Relationships, Social Connection, and Work & Life Flow." path="/framework">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-dark" style="overflow:hidden">
    <div class="glow" style="left:-20%;top:-35%;width:70%;background:radial-gradient(closest-side,rgba(217,234,110,.13),rgba(217,234,110,0) 70%)"></div>
    <div class="wrap split" style="padding-top:clamp(48px,7vw,96px);padding-bottom:clamp(120px,14vw,190px)">
      <div style="max-width:600px">
        <span class="eyebrow">The framework</span>
        <h1 style="color:var(--on-dark)">The Five Pillars of <span class="mk mk-d">Fulfilment</span>.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Human wellbeing isn’t one idea. It’s five distinct, connected parts of life. Strengthen them all, and everything changes.</p>
        <div class="btns">
          <a class="btn btn-lime" href="#explore">Explore the pillars</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/fulfilment-check-in">Take the check-in</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-fig">
        <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:5/4;box-shadow:0 50px 90px -40px rgba(0,0,0,.7)"><img src="/assets/happy-participants.jpg" alt="A large group of workshop participants celebrating together outdoors" width="1024" height="683" style="object-position:50% 60%" /></div>
        <figcaption class="hero-chip">
          <span class="hero-dots">{PILLARS.map(p => <span style={`background:${p.tint}`}><Icon paths={p.paths} size={18} stroke="#14231A" width={1.6} /></span>)}</span>
          <span>Five pillars, one life</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why the framework exists: half the picture, or the whole person. -->
  <section class="lift" style="background:var(--cream)">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="narrow center">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why it exists</span>
        <h2>Most wellbeing thinking starts in <span class="mk">the wrong place</span>.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="vs">
        <figure class="card vs-a" data-rv>
          <span class="pill">The usual approach</span>
          <div class="vs-dots" role="img" aria-label="Only one of the five pillars, Work & Life Flow, is looked at">
            {PILLARS.map((p, i) => <span class={i === 4 ? 'lit' : 'off'} style={`--t:${p.tint}`}><Icon paths={p.paths} size={20} stroke="#14231A" width={1.5} /></span>)}
          </div>
          <h3>Fix the workplace, fix the person.</h3>
          <p class="body">Stress at work. Performance at work. Engagement at work. A model that only looks at the job is working with <b>half the picture</b>.</p>
        </figure>
        <span class="vs-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow" size={22} /></span>
        <figure class="card-dark vs-b" data-rv>
          <span class="pill">The Five Pillars</span>
          <div class="vs-dots" role="img" aria-label="All five pillars are looked at together">
            {PILLARS.map(p => <span class="lit" style={`--t:${p.tint}`}><Icon paths={p.paths} size={20} stroke="#14231A" width={1.5} /></span>)}
          </div>
          <h3>Start with the whole human.</h3>
          <p class="body">What happens at home shapes how someone shows up in the morning. Their relationships, purpose and energy all come to work with them. None of it stops at the door.</p>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="split why" style="align-items:start">
        <figure class="big-q" data-rv>
          <svg class="q-mark" width="44" height="33" viewBox="0 0 64 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 48V28C0 12 8 3 24 0l3 6C17 9 13 15 12.5 22H26v26zm36 0V28c0-16 8-25 24-28l3 6c-10 3-14 9-14.5 16H62v26z" /></svg>
          <blockquote>Crisis rarely appears out of nowhere. It sits downstream from <span class="mk">prolonged disconnection</span>: from self, from others, from a meaningful way of living.</blockquote>
        </figure>
        <div>
          <div class="accs">
            <details class="acc">
              <summary><span class="ico"><Icon name="search" size={22} /></span><span>Why most programs fall short<span class="acc-sub">Good intentions, incomplete model</span></span></summary>
              <div class="acc-body"><p>Most wellbeing programs produce limited results. Not because the people behind them don’t care, but because the model they’re using only sees the workplace. The quality of someone’s closest relationships decides their emotional bandwidth. Their sense of purpose, or the absence of it, affects every decision they make. Their physical energy either fuels or drains everything else they attempt.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="acc">
              <summary><span class="ico"><Icon name="heart" size={22} /></span><span>Seen, not assessed<span class="acc-sub">Honest, accessible and actionable</span></span></summary>
              <div class="acc-body"><p>The Five Pillars of Fulfilment starts with the whole human, not just the employee, and gives people a structured, practical way to see where their life is under pressure and what to do about it. It was never designed as a clinical or diagnostic tool. It was designed to be honest, accessible and actionable, so people feel seen rather than assessed.</p></div>
            </details>
            <details class="acc">
              <summary><span class="ico"><Icon name="globe" size={22} /></span><span>Built for this moment<span class="acc-sub">Change has outpaced us</span></span></summary>
              <div class="acc-body"><p>Change has moved faster than people have adapted to it. AI is reshaping work. Remote and hybrid work have dissolved the line between professional and personal life. Digital communication has made us more reachable and, oddly, more alone. The Five Pillars were built for exactly this moment.</p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
          <a class="link" href="/what-we-do">See how we deliver it in practice ›</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The explorer: pick a pillar on the pentagon, see its depth. -->
  <section id="explore" class="bg-sand lift-b" style="scroll-margin-top:40px">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="split" style="align-items:end">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">The Five Pillars</span><h2>Five dimensions of <span class="mk">a whole life</span>.</h2></div>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:0">Each pillar is a part of life that shows up at work whether anyone talks about it or not. Pick one to see what it covers, and how it pulls on the other four.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="px" data-tabs>
        <div class="px-side">
          <div class="px-wheel" role="tablist" aria-label="The Five Pillars of Fulfilment">
            <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${PX.w} ${PX.h}`} aria-hidden="true">
              <polygon points={svgPts(pxC)} fill="rgba(250,248,240,.6)" stroke="none" />
              {pxLines.map(l => <line class:list={['ln', `ln-${l.a}`, `ln-${l.b}`, { dg: !l.edge }]} x1={pxC[l.a][0]} y1={pxC[l.a][1]} x2={pxC[l.b][0]} y2={pxC[l.b][1]} />)}
              <rect x={PX.cx - 80} y={PX.cy - 18} width="160" height="64" rx="28" fill="#F5F3EA" />
              <text x={PX.cx} y={PX.cy + 14} text-anchor="middle" font-family="'DM Serif Display', Georgia, serif" font-size="28" fill="#14231A">Fulfilment</text>
              <text x={PX.cx} y={PX.cy + 35} text-anchor="middle" font-family="'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="2" fill="#4A6B3A">PICK A PILLAR</text>
            </svg>
            {pillars.map((p, i) => (
              <button type="button" class="px-b" role="tab" id={`px-t${i}`} aria-controls={`px-p${i}`} style={`left:${pct(pxC[i][0], PX.w)};top:${pct(pxC[i][1], PX.h)};--t:${p.tint}`}>
                <span class="px-dot"><Icon paths={p.paths} size={26} stroke="#14231A" width={1.5} /></span>
                <span class="px-l">{p.name}</span>
              </button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <p class="px-hint small">The lines show how the pillar you pick connects to the other four.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-panels">
          {pillars.map((p, i) => (
            <article class="card px-p" role="tabpanel" id={`px-p${i}`} aria-labelledby={`px-t${i}`} style={`--t:${p.tint}`}>
              <div class="px-hd">
                <span class="px-badge"><Icon paths={p.paths} size={28} stroke="#14231A" width={1.5} /></span>
                <div><span class="eyebrow">Pillar 0{i + 1} of 5</span><h3>{p.name}</h3></div>
              </div>
              <p class="px-intro">{p.intro}</p>
              <p class="body">{p.body[0]}</p>
              <h4 class="px-k">What this looks like in practice</h4>
              <ul class="px-pr">{p.practices.map(t => <li><Icon name="check" size={16} width={2} />{t}</li>)}</ul>
              <div class="accs px-more">
                <details class="acc">
                  <summary>Go deeper on {p.name}</summary>
                  <div class="acc-body">{p.body.slice(1).map(t => <p>{t}</p>)}</div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- One system: what it sounds like, and what is really going on. -->
  <section class="lift" style="background:var(--cream)">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="split" style="align-items:end">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">How they connect</span><h2>Five pillars. <span class="mk">One system.</span></h2></div>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:0">Each pillar shapes the others, often in ways that stay invisible until you know what to look for. Here’s what it sounds like at work, and what’s really going on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sys" data-tabs>
        <div class="tablist sys-says" role="tablist" aria-label="What it sounds like at work">
          {EXAMPLES.map((e, i) => (
            <button type="button" class="say" role="tab" id={`sys-t${i}`} aria-controls={`sys-p${i}`}><Icon name="talk" size={22} /><span>{e.says}</span></button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="sys-panels">
          {EXAMPLES.map((e, i) => (
            <div class="card sys-p" role="tabpanel" id={`sys-p${i}`} aria-labelledby={`sys-t${i}`}>
              <span class="eyebrow">What’s really going on</span>
              <ol class="chain" aria-label={'How it travels: ' + e.chain.map(k => PILLARS[k].name).join(', then ')}>
                {e.chain.map(k => (
                  <li style={`--t:${PILLARS[k].tint}`}><span class="c-dot"><Icon paths={PILLARS[k].paths} size={24} stroke="#14231A" width={1.5} /></span><b>{PILLARS[k].name}</b></li>
                ))}
              </ol>
              <p class="body">{e.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The line that sums it up. -->
  <section class="band lift-b">
    <div class="wrap sec-tight">
      <figure class="band-q" data-rv>
        <svg class="q-mark" width="56" height="42" viewBox="0 0 64 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 48V28C0 12 8 3 24 0l3 6C17 9 13 15 12.5 22H26v26zm36 0V28c0-16 8-25 24-28l3 6c-10 3-14 9-14.5 16H62v26z" /></svg>
        <blockquote>Strengthen one pillar, and you strengthen the others. Neglect one, and <span class="mk mk-w">the rest start to crack</span>.</blockquote>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Where are you right now? The Fulfilment Score. -->
  <section class="bg-dark lift">
    <div class="glow" style="right:-14%;bottom:-30%;width:56%;background:radial-gradient(closest-side,rgba(217,234,110,.12),rgba(217,234,110,0) 70%)"></div>
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="split ci" style="align-items:center">
        <div style="flex:1 1 440px;max-width:600px">
          <span class="eyebrow">The Fulfilment Score</span>
          <h2>Where are you <span class="mk mk-d">right now</span>?</h2>
          <p class="lead">Every engagement with us begins here: an honest pulse check across all Five Pillars. Not a personality quiz, not a clinical diagnostic. A clear picture of where you are.</p>
          <ul class="ci-stats">
            <li><b>20</b><span>questions</span></li>
            <li><b>5</b><span>pillars</span></li>
            <li><b>4</b><span>minutes or so</span></li>
            <li><b>1</b><span>clear starting point</span></li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-lime" href="/fulfilment-check-in">Take the free check-in</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/what-we-do/norma">Track it with nørma</a></div>
        </div>
        <a class="ci-card" href="/fulfilment-check-in" data-rv>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 320" role="img" aria-label="An example Fulfilment check-in result: a shape across the Five Pillars, strong in some and with room to grow in others">
            {ciRings.map(r => <polygon points={r} fill="none" stroke="rgba(228,240,214,.13)" stroke-width="1" />)}
            {pts(CI.cx, CI.cy, () => CI.r).map(([x, yy]) => <line x1={CI.cx} y1={CI.cy} x2={x} y2={yy} stroke="rgba(228,240,214,.1)" stroke-width="1" />)}
            <polygon class="ci-shape" points={svgPts(ciShape)} fill="rgba(217,234,110,.24)" stroke="#D9EA6E" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" />
            {ciShape.map(([x, yy]) => <circle class="ci-shape" cx={x} cy={yy} r="3.5" fill="#D9EA6E" />)}
            {PILLARS.map((p, i) => (
              <g>
                <circle cx={ciIcons[i][0]} cy={ciIcons[i][1]} r="18" fill={p.tint} />
                <g transform={`translate(${(ciIcons[i][0] - 10).toFixed(1)} ${(ciIcons[i][1] - 10).toFixed(1)}) scale(.8333)`} fill="none" stroke="#14231A" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">{p.paths.map(d => <path d={d} />)}</g>
              </g>
            ))}
          </svg>
          <span class="ci-go"><span>Free · about four minutes · no sign-up</span><b>Find your shape <Icon name="arrow" size={18} width={2} /></b></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps ci-steps" style="--n:3">
        <li><h3>Answer twenty questions</h3><p class="body">Honest, quick, and across all five pillars of your life.</p></li>
        <li><h3>See your picture</h3><p class="body">Where you’re strong, and the pillar with the most room to grow.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Take it to everyone with nørma</h3><p class="body">Wellbeing at scale: every person tracks their score privately, and leaders see it in aggregate across every team.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="accs ci-acc">
        <details class="acc">
          <summary><span class="ico"><Icon name="users" size={22} /></span><span>Why leadership teams take it together<span class="acc-sub">A shared language, and a baseline</span></span></summary>
          <div class="acc-body"><p>The score creates a shared language. When a leadership team completes it together, they get a common reference point for conversations that are often too uncomfortable to start without one. It also creates a baseline, so progress becomes visible and change becomes measurable.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The framework in action -->
  <section class="bg-sand lift-b">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="split" style="align-items:end">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">The framework in action</span><h2>The backbone of <span class="mk">everything we deliver</span>.</h2></div>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:0">One room, one team or one leader at a time, every format works from the same Five Pillars. nørma takes them to everyone: wellbeing at scale.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="track">
        {FORMATS.map(f => (
          <li data-rv>
            <a href={f.href}>
              <span class="t-node"><Icon name={f.icon} size={24} /></span>
              <span class="pill">{f.tag}</span>
              <h3>{f.title}</h3>
              <p class="body">{f.text}</p>
              <span class="link">Find out more ›</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
        <li data-rv class="t-norma">
          <a href="/what-we-do/norma">
            <span class="t-node"><img src="/assets/norma-app-icon.png" alt="" width="48" height="48" /></span>
            <span class="pill">At scale</span>
            <h3>nørma</h3>
            <p class="body">Wellbeing at scale: every person and every team, every month.</p>
            <span class="link">Meet nørma ›</span>
          </a>
        </li>
